---
description: USE WHEN creating a branch, pushing for review, or opening a merge request (MR) or pull request
alwaysApply: false
---

## Always use a merge request

Do **not** assume **`git push`** to **`main`** (or default branch) will succeed. **Protected branches** are common. After commit:

1. Use a **feature branch** (see naming below), **`git push -u origin <branch>`**.
2. Open an **MR** (GitLab) / **PR** (GitHub): **`POST /git/mr`** when **`/health`** passes (**`CONTRIBUTING.md`**); else **`gh pr create`** where applicable, or give the user the **new MR URL** from the remote (e.g. GitLab “create merge request” link).

## Branch naming (JIRA required)

Pattern:

**`{type}/{JIRA-KEY}-{short-kebab-description}`**

- **`type`:** same idea as Conventional Commits — **`feat`**, **`fix`** (use for bugs), **`chore`**, **`docs`**, **`refactor`**, **`test`**, **`perf`**, **`ci`**.
- **`JIRA-KEY`:** real tracker key, e.g. **`CRUX-42`**, **`PROJ-123`** (project prefix + number).
- **`short-kebab-description`:** a few words, lowercase, hyphens.

Examples: **`feat/CRUX-12-elevenlabs-tls-options`**, **`fix/PROJ-99-guard-speak-route`**.

## If JIRA is missing

If the user (or task) did **not** provide a JIRA issue key, **ask for it before** choosing the branch name or pushing. Do not invent keys.

Details and HTTP examples: **`CONTRIBUTING.md`** (branches + **`POST /git/mr`**).
